From: pocket_vm developers <pocket-vm@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] um: keep the kernel FP-state types on old glibc

glibc up to 2.17 declares the signal FP-state structures itself and pulls
them in through <sys/ucontext.h>; from 2.18 it leaves them to the kernel
header.  Including <asm/sigcontext.h> afterwards therefore redefines five
structures on exactly those older hosts.

Rename the kernel's copies on the way in -- the same trick this file already
uses for struct sigcontext -- and keep the aliases in place afterwards, so
the file goes on reading the kernel layout.  That matters beyond the name
clash: get_fpstate() reads the sw_reserved area, which the kernel structure
has and the old glibc one does not.

<bits/sigcontext.h> defining its own include guard is the exact signal that
its declarations arrived, so no version test is needed.
---
 arch/x86/um/os-Linux/mcontext.c | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/x86/um/os-Linux/mcontext.c b/arch/x86/um/os-Linux/mcontext.c
index b1580df..83a4c08 100644
--- a/arch/x86/um/os-Linux/mcontext.c
+++ b/arch/x86/um/os-Linux/mcontext.c
@@ -9,6 +9,23 @@
  * copy to avoid redefinition while keeping the FP-state types available.
  */
 #define sigcontext __kernel_sigcontext
+/*
+ * glibc up to 2.17 declares the signal FP-state structures itself and pulls
+ * them in through <sys/ucontext.h>; from 2.18 it leaves them to the kernel
+ * header, which is why this collides on old hosts only. Rename the kernel's
+ * copies the same way, then keep the aliases in place for the rest of the
+ * file: get_fpstate() reads the sw_reserved area, which exists in the kernel
+ * layout and not in the old glibc one, so the kernel definition is the one
+ * this file has to be looking at. <bits/sigcontext.h> having defined its own
+ * include guard is the exact signal that its declarations arrived.
+ */
+#ifdef _BITS_SIGCONTEXT_H
+#define _fpx_sw_bytes	__kernel_fpx_sw_bytes
+#define _fpstate	__kernel_fpstate
+#define _xsave_hdr	__kernel_xsave_hdr
+#define _ymmh_state	__kernel_ymmh_state
+#define _xstate		__kernel_xstate
+#endif
 #include <asm/sigcontext.h>
 #undef sigcontext
 #include <sysdep/ptrace.h>
